  partName: Oil Pan Bolt (2)
  description: The Oil Pan Bolt (2) is another tiny, complex-shaped component situated
    at the bottom-left-front of the engine, also made of Material.001, and serves
    a similar purpose to the Oil Pan Bolt. By securing the oil pan in place, it helps
    maintain the engine's lubrication system and prevent potential damage from oil
    leaks or spills. An interesting aspect of the Oil Pan Bolt (2) is its potential
    for being used in conjunction with other fasteners to provide additional security
    and reinforcement, depending on the specific engine design and manufacturer specifications.
